# Line-ending normalisation.
#
# This repository is authored on Windows but is consumed on every platform, so
# text is stored LF-only in the object database and checked out with LF
# everywhere. Without this, the first cross-machine checkout rewrites every file
# and produces whitespace-only diffs.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files are the exception: cmd.exe parses them line by line, and
# LF-only batch files can misbehave around labels and `goto`. They are stored
# LF-normalised in the object database (like every other text file) but checked
# out with CRLF in the working tree, which is the form the script interpreter
# expects.
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: never apply line-ending conversion and never diff as text.
# The WFDB extensions are listed for completeness even though data/raw/ is
# gitignored and must never be committed.
*.onnx binary
*.dat binary
*.atr binary
*.xws binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
